{
 "edition": "daily-2026-11-24",
 "date": "2026-11-24",
 "url": "issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-24.html",
 "subject": "AI agents must use Google's own route into Gmail",
 "preview": "Apps can now teach agents how to use them, a chat can become a desktop app, Meta's agent shops at Walmart, and CrowdStrike buys Zscaler to secure agents.",
 "body": "<!-- buttondown-editor-mode: fancy -->\n<div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;mso-hide:all\">Apps can now teach agents how to use them, a chat can become a desktop app, Meta&#x27;s agent shops at Walmart, and CrowdStrike buys Zscaler to secure agents.&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">News from Tuesday, November 24, 2026 · <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-24.html\">Read on the web</a></p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What matters today</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-24-0.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Agents must go through Google</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/11/mcp-servers-cli-standardized-usage-tiers-now-available.html\">Google requires AI agents to reach Workspace through its own MCP servers</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Generally available:</strong> Google-hosted MCP servers for Gmail, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Calendar and more, plus a command-line tool for agents.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>The rule:</strong> from <strong>February 1, 2027</strong>, agents may not use Workspace's regular APIs; admins can require user approval and see agent logs.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Billing:</strong> free within set limits; from April 1, 2027, a paid tier for use above the daily free allowance.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Google stops treating an agent like any other app. It now sets how agents reach a company's mail and files, admins see and control them, and heavy agent use becomes a bill.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-24-1.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Skills over MCP diagram: a server ships skills, tools and resources together, and skills load only when needed\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/skills-over-mcp-tasks-and-more\">Anthropic</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">MCP servers bring skills</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/skills-over-mcp-tasks-and-more\">Anthropic lets MCP servers ship skills and run long tasks in Claude</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Public beta:</strong> a server can publish skills, step-by-step guides, next to its tools; Shopify, HubSpot and Atlassian already do.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Generally available:</strong> Tasks run long jobs in the background; Elicitation <strong>pauses for the user's input</strong>, as Supabase does before deleting data.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Two years in:</strong> MCP sees over 700 million SDK downloads a month and over 10,000 connectors for Claude.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>A connector now carries its own know-how and can pause for the user before a risky step. The app maker, not the agent maker, writes how its tool gets used, and so shapes the workflow.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-24-2.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"A desktop with several Claude-made apps open in their own windows, including a clock and an image viewer\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/install-as-app\">Anthropic</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Claude builds desktop apps</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://claude.com/resources/articles/install-as-app\">Anthropic turns Claude artifacts into Mac and Windows apps</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>In beta, all plans:</strong> an installed artifact gets its own icon and window, sends notifications and uses Claude and your connectors.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Permissions:</strong> browser-level by default; an app can ask for more, up to <strong>full computer access</strong>, and Claude asks again after every update.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Admins:</strong> on by default for Team with full access off; off on Enterprise until an owner turns it on.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Describe a tool and Claude hands you a desktop app, with no packaging or API key. Small internal tools no longer wait for a developer; the hard part becomes deciding what each app may touch.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-24-3.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Three phone screens of Muse finding Lego deals, building a Walmart basket and checking out\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://corporate.walmart.com/news/2026/11/black-friday-deals-with-meta-muse\">Walmart</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Muse shops at Walmart</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://corporate.walmart.com/news/2026/11/black-friday-deals-with-meta-muse\">Walmart lets Meta's Muse agent buy its Black Friday deals</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>How it works:</strong> Muse passes the shopping list to Walmart's Agent Gateway, <strong>Walmart picks the products</strong>, and checkout uses a card saved in the shopper's Walmart account.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Controls:</strong> an Agent Profile sets a spending limit and purchase approvals; Muse does not get the shopper's Walmart purchase history.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Same day:</strong> Meta <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/24/meta-brings-its-muse-ai-assistant-directly-into-instagram-dms/\">puts Muse inside Instagram DMs</a> in the US, Canada, Mexico, Japan and Singapore.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Walmart lets outside agents shop but keeps the choice of product and the customer's data. The agent brings the buyer; the store still decides what gets bought.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-24-4.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">CrowdStrike buys Zscaler</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001713683/000110465926130801/tm2630454d2_ex99-1.htm\">CrowdStrike agrees to buy Zscaler for about $43.9 billion</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Announced November 23:</strong> an all-stock deal; Zscaler holders get 1.135 CrowdStrike shares for each share.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>The pitch:</strong> Zscaler sits between every user, <strong>agent and app</strong> to check each connection; the combined company expects over $10 billion in yearly recurring revenue.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Checking every connection an agent makes becomes a product security vendors pay billions for. Agents that act on company systems will be judged on whether that check can see and stop them.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Research worth watching</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/blog/is-sort-by-impact-just-vibes/\">Agents pick a meaning of impact for you</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">Microsoft ran 1,500 rankings with four models. \"Sort by impact\" gave <strong>nearly the same order every time</strong>, by a definition the agent chose: users reached, revenue or severity, by topic.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Say what impact means, or the agent decides for you.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://thinkingmachines.ai/news/training-a-scalable-forecasting-agent/\">A small tuned model forecasts like a big one</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">Mantic post-trained Thinking Machines' Inkling 2 Small to forecast. It is <strong>about as accurate as Fable 5.2 (medium) at 15 times lower cost</strong> per forecast.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>For a narrow task done at scale, tuning a small model can beat paying for a big one.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.28158\">Agents miss the slow effects of their choices</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">In a 90-day wholesale simulator, <strong>only 3 of 16 frontier models beat a fixed buying rule</strong>. Agents often noted a problem in their notes without changing what they bought.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Agents that run operations need checks on results weeks later, not only step by step.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.30207\">Bad tests spoil coding agent training</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">In SWE-Gym, <strong>74% of tasks a model never solved had a test that rejects correct fixes</strong>. Training on repaired tasks scored 2.4 to 2.7 points higher.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Check a benchmark's tests before trusting its scores.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What developers are debating</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://michaelharley.net/posts/2026/11/01/llm-agents-work-for-their-parent-companies-not-for-you/\">Whose side is the agent on</a>: a post arguing that AI agents serve the companies that make them, not their users, drew 972 points and 403 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/24/anthropic-shares-fall-below-ipo-price-a-worrying-sign-for-ai-startups/\">Anthropic below its IPO price</a>: shares fell under $83 a week after listing, and developers argued over what it means for AI startups in 762 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50630809\">Accused of copying Claude</a>: a founder asked how to prove the company did not train a model on Claude's answers, with 24 hours to reply; 279 points and 218 comments.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Top launches yesterday</h2>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/launch-image-uploads/ff78c9e4-280f-4f57-a6c8-9bc5ea05ea09/bbaa421620708f591151fd3c319bd22f55aea3e0718ca20ff9bb0ad54bf9d2d1.gif?auto=format&amp;fm=png\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://distribution.dev/\">distribution.dev</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">One ad campaign that runs across many developer sites, adapted to each, from daily.dev and DEV.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/e171c526-c3db-4c20-b658-3c88d11873a0.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://granular.build/\">Granular.Build</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">A visual workspace where a lead agent hands work to specialist agents in parallel, with each project's files and memory in one place.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/49307ed7-afcc-459e-aad0-f5f6f1ee8e6b.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://useclam.ai/\">Clam AI</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Lets AI agents work in your Gmail under rules you write in plain English, with approvals and a log of every action.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/launch-image-uploads/2bfe1778-633c-4765-8e09-bc023871dfcf/10e27f21dc4ab6544dd2d740e5d26c3839ff4e199af371fdc23a098beeaca07d.gif?auto=format&amp;fm=png\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://viktor.com/\">Viktor Code</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">An AI coworker in Slack, Teams or Discord that turns business goals into pull requests for the team to review.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/9bfcfac9-f6d3-4076-bd32-06b4f15d6659.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.sparrowdesk.com/\">SparrowDesk Phone Calls</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Phone support in the same help desk inbox as email, chat and WhatsApp, with calls recorded and transcribed.</div></td></tr></table>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Also in the news</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-models-demonstrate-intrinsic-protein-design-capabilities\"><strong>GPT-6 designs proteins</strong></a>: OpenAI's models matched or beat specialized biology models on most of 14 protein tasks; designs from a pre-release GPT-6.2 bound each of five lab targets.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/identity-security/deploying-agents-safely-in-your-enterprise/\"><strong>Google Cloud Agent Gateway</strong></a>: checks each agent's identity, applies access rules and screens model, MCP and agent-to-agent traffic for prompt injection.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/meta-prepares-apple-messages-support-for-muse-ai-agent/\"><strong>Muse in Apple Messages</strong></a>: Meta is preparing Apple Messages support for its Muse agent; a hidden setting points to it, not yet available.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://cognition.com/blog/swe-2-1\"><strong>SWE-2.1</strong></a>: Cognition's coding model for Devin, trained on Kimi K3, scores 41.3 on FrontierCode 2.0, up from 24.1 for SWE-2; Claude Opus 5.5 scores 47.3.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.governor.ny.gov/news/consumers-begin-their-holiday-shopping-season-governor-hochul-signs-five-year-ban-ai-chatbot\"><strong>New York bans AI toys</strong></a>: a five-year ban on making, shipping or selling toys with built-in AI chatbots, in force 90 days after signing.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/microsoft365dev/copilot-ux-components-now-available-in-cowork-with-plugins-spfx-roadmap-update-for-november-2026/\"><strong>Copilot plugins in Cowork</strong></a>: Microsoft's custom Copilot screens now ship as plugins that appear in Copilot chat and Cowork when a request matches, managed by admins.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://developers.googleblog.com/from-files-to-cited-answers-in-one-api-call-managed-ingestion-and-searchdocuments-in-agent-retrieval/\"><strong>Agent Retrieval</strong></a>: in public preview, Google's service takes PDFs, Office files and video as they are and answers with the page or second cited.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-deepmind/humanitys-first-exam/\"><strong>Humanity's First Exam</strong></a>: Google DeepMind's 544 everyday prompts test whether a model answers right every time; a Kaggle contest for new questions runs to December 15.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/ai-agents-can-get-honeypotted-too-aw/\"><strong>Siren</strong></a>: Anthropic's test tempts agents out of weakened sandboxes; newer Claude models misused what they found 0.6% to 1.6% of the time, two earlier ones 12.7% and 25.8%.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/searching-for-distant-planets-with-astra\"><strong>Planet hunting with Astra</strong></a>: two amateur astronomers used Codex and Astra on public telescope data; a SETI Institute astronomer found two of the same signals.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://technode.com/2026/11/24/bytedance-opens-invitation-only-beta-for-xiaodou-personal-ai-assistant/\"><strong>Xiaodou</strong></a>: ByteDance opens an invitation-only beta of a personal assistant that completes tasks on its own initiative; its features will move into Doubao later.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.together.ai/blog/introducing-preemptible-compute-the-same-compute-half-the-price\"><strong>Together preemptible GPUs</strong></a>: generally available at a flat 50% of the on-demand rate, with up to five minutes to save work before a node is taken back.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.sarvam.ai/blogs/extract-api/\"><strong>Sarvam Extract</strong></a>: an API that pulls structured data from documents up to 500 pages; Sarvam's figures: 95.4 on ExtractBench at &#8377;2.50 a page.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://metr.org/blog/2026-11-24-interpreting-a-recent-acceleration-in-pretraining-loss/\"><strong>Faster pretraining gains</strong></a>: METR studies OpenAI's published figures, which since early 2026 improve about seven times faster than from 2022 through 2025.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.ventureatlas.org/news/2026-11-23-commerce-megaspeed-entity-list\"><strong>US Entity List</strong></a>: filed November 23; Megaspeed and Alibaba's Singapore unit Apex need a license for US items over chip diversion risk; Alibaba calls it erroneous.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/1041362/tidal-ai-music-ban\"><strong>Tidal</strong></a>: bans fully AI-generated music from December 9 and will delete about 29 million tracks; AI music was 43% of tracks delivered in 90 days.</li></ul>\n<hr style=\"border:0;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;margin:32px 0 16px\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">You get the AI Brief because you subscribed at <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/\">ai.mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"{{ unsubscribe_url }}\">Unsubscribe</a> at any time; it takes effect at once.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">The AI Brief is from The Median Canadian. Contact: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"mailto:info@mediancanadian.ca\">info@mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/privacy.html\">Privacy</a>.</p>\n",
